                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]The Dinos are Derpy, but the project is made with love![/h1]\n\n[i]Derpy Dinos[/i] is an indie game that was born from the result of a school project that focuses on a 2D danmaku shooter similar to [i]R-Type[/i], but without all the sci-fi action.  It instead takes a safer route by portraying itself as a casual game that's easy to pick up and play.  Though it doesn't seem that fascinating on the surface, I found myself intrigued by the \"orbit\" system implemented.\n\nThe gameplay is simple, yet enjoyable.  It focuses on your main character, an alien spaceship aiming to destroy all humans (tourists and natives), dinosaurs (with mounted guns to provide a bit of a challenge if you're aiming for those achievements), and an active volcano's boulders.  The more entertaining part of the gameplay was using the tractor beam to collect various objects as ammo and sending them into orbit...but watch out, your ammo might hit you if you're not careful!  Of course, the most quirky aspect of this game is the destruction of the targets, where villagers will explode into villager heads and dinosaurs will explode into several copies of their own heads.\n\nThe music is nothing special and is what you'd expect from a casual game and a class project, but the sound effects are quite fitting.  Sadly, the game's scope is limited by its own simplicity, without having room for growth.  You may find yourself getting bored after a while of playing as you'll essentially see more of the same from wave to wave.  At this point, you'll be grinding (or challenging yourself) to get those achievements.  Speaking of which, one of the developers of this project has been kind enough to reduce some of the kill caps on the kill achievements, making them a little more fair to get.  A friendly staff helps the game's image.\n\nFrankly, despite the limited scope, I recommend [i]Derpy Dinos[/i] if you're an achievement hunter or if you're simply looking for a casual game to settle down with.  It should take you around 5-6 hours to get all achievements of this game.  Try not to take this game too seriously, it's a school project and a casual experience.\n\n6/10  Though the Dinos are Derpy, this game isn't too Derpy at all.",
